course: dictionary
lesson: 9535
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. The word stock is a good example. «A shop has 50 tins in stock» means goods kept there to sell. Read the words around it and ask: what would fit here?
explain: Try the meaning in the sentence. In «Stock is the things a business keeps to sell or use», the clue is business, so stock means goods a business keeps. In a recipe, «chicken stock» is cooking, so stock is a liquid made by boiling meat or vegetables for soup. Same word, different meaning.
explain: Be careful with stocks, with an s. In «The stock market is a place where people buy and sell shares», it means shares: small parts of companies. Stock can also be a verb, as in shopkeepers who stock the shelves. Check the clue words before you decide.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: One word can have several meanings, and context shows which one is being used.
fact: «Stock» can mean goods kept in a shop, a liquid for soup, or farm animals.
fact: «Stocks», with an s, can mean shares: small parts of a company that people buy and sell.
fact: «In stock» means available to buy; «out of stock» means none left to sell.
exercise: «A shop has 50 tins in stock and sells 18.» What does stock mean here? | *Goods kept in a shop to sell | Shares in a company | A liquid for soup | A wooden frame used for punishment
exercise: In a recipe, «Add a cup of chicken stock to the pan.» What is the stock? | A stock answer in a test | A plant that grows in gardens | Farm animals on a hill | *A liquid made by boiling meat, bones or vegetables
exercise: «The stock market is a place where people buy and sell shares.» What are stocks in this sentence? | Old stories told by the grown-ups | Wooden frames used for punishment | Animals on a farm | *Small parts of companies that people buy and sell
test: In «Stock is the things a business keeps to sell or use», which clue word tells you stock means goods? | Sing | Laughing | *Business | Whisper
test: Luis reads «Please stock up on bread before the storm.» What does stock up mean? | To fall in price | *To buy and keep a supply of something | To boil bones for soup | To laugh at someone
exam: The shelves are empty and the sign says «out of stock». What does this mean? | The usual goods are on sale | The shop only sells soup | *There are none left to sell | The shop has shares in a company
